                "entry_id": "39106d63-03c2-33cb-84a5-305e7ff3d31d",
                "word": "scientiste",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "c5bec1e1-a8af-470b-b88d-42b0b57444fb",
                        "entry_id": "39106d63-03c2-33cb-84a5-305e7ff3d31d",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "masculine",
                            "feminine"
                        ],
                        "form": "scientistes"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b324e237-9a1f-3c51-bc3f-c99fb3a9bdc6",
                        "entry_id": "39106d63-03c2-33cb-84a5-305e7ff3d31d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Relatif au scientisme."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e0290bf8-f8f9-4cba-bb04-1d446b5d2905",
                                "sense_id": "b324e237-9a1f-3c51-bc3f-c99fb3a9bdc6",
                                "text": "Le positivisme scientiste."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9d9ea219-75d8-4c97-b4e1-1af3bc46c6a6",
                                "sense_id": "b324e237-9a1f-3c51-bc3f-c99fb3a9bdc6",
                                "text": "Disons que la psychanalyse se voit aujourd’hui assiégée, contestée, invalidée même par tous ceux qui – dans une optique plutôt scientiste – pensent que les troubles psychiques ne relèvent que du biologique, c’est-à-dire de la chimie."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "83a7550b-8af1-4803-bf3d-833c69c3c4fa",
                                "sense_id": "b324e237-9a1f-3c51-bc3f-c99fb3a9bdc6",
                                "text": "La discipline économique feint parfois d’être devenue purement « scientifique » et de se soucier uniquement d’une mesure objective de « l’efficacité productive ». En pratique, cette posture scientiste et productiviste sert depuis longtemps à dissimuler une idéologie sociale conservatrice reposant sur la sacralisation du marché, de la propriété et de l’inégalité."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "7f8982b5-3023-4c7e-b194-9e1aa66bf8aa",
                        "source_entry_id": "39106d63-03c2-33cb-84a5-305e7ff3d31d",
                        "source_sense_id": "b324e237-9a1f-3c51-bc3f-c99fb3a9bdc6",
                        "target_lang_word": "scientist",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "scientist",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3c4c7506-9ac6-3380-bf27-5c96c3659908",
                                        "entry_id": "b2c45f0d-6cf2-361d-bde6-f7fbac256a15",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One whose activities make use of the scientific method to answer questions regarding the measurable universe. A scientist may be involved in original research, or make use of the results of the research of others."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bbb67ca3-2343-4417-8e2a-10ef6e496599",
                                                "sense_id": "3c4c7506-9ac6-3380-bf27-5c96c3659908",
                                                "text": "As we cannot use physician for a cultivator of physics, I have called him a physicist. We need very much a name to describe a cultivator of science in general. I should incline to call him a Scientist. Thus we might say, that as an Artist is a Musician, Painter, or Poet, a Scientist is a Mathematician, Physicist, or Naturalist."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6b1f4b58-aea1-4cf4-80b4-6970880e780f",
                                                "sense_id": "3c4c7506-9ac6-3380-bf27-5c96c3659908",
                                                "text": "Becoming more aware of the progress that scientists have made on behavioral fronts can reduce the risk that other natural scientists will resort to mystical agential accounts when they exceed the limits of their own disciplinary training."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "eb2c6408-533e-40f3-839c-b536627d3ffd",
                                                "sense_id": "3c4c7506-9ac6-3380-bf27-5c96c3659908",
                                                "text": "The US supreme court has ruled unanimously that natural human genes cannot be patented, a decision that scientists and civil rights campaigners said removed a major barrier to patient care and medical innovation."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b6246626-45e0-43c7-a520-e69ec959fffe",
                        "source_entry_id": "39106d63-03c2-33cb-84a5-305e7ff3d31d",
                        "source_sense_id": "b324e237-9a1f-3c51-bc3f-c99fb3a9bdc6",
